/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Numbers chapters 26-30
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("numbers", [
{n:26, name:"The Second Census", seal:{ref:"Numbers 26:65",verse:"For the LORD had said of them, They shall surely die in the wilderness. And there was not left a man of them, save Caleb the son of Jephunneh, and Joshua the son of Nun."}, facts:["Did you know the second census counted 601,730 fighting men, only about 1,800 fewer than the 603,550 counted at Sinai nearly forty years earlier (Numbers 1:46; 26:51)?","Did you know the children of Korah did not die with their father in his rebellion, and their descendants later became some of Israel's psalm writers (Numbers 26:11)?","Did you know that of all the men counted in the first census, only Caleb and Joshua were still alive to be counted in the second (Numbers 26:65)?"], questions:[
{q:"When did the LORD command this second census?", options:["After the plague","After the golden calf was destroyed","After Aaron died on Mount Hor","After the defeat of Sihon, king of the Amorites"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:1",verse:"And it came to pass after the plague, that the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest, saying,", insight:"God numbers His people afresh after judgment; the plague had cleared the ground, and grace began again."},
{q:"Who was to be counted in this census?", options:["Every male from twenty years old and upward, all able to go to war","Every firstborn son of every tribe","Every Levite from a month old and upward","Every woman and child over twelve"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:2",verse:"Take the sum of all the congregation of the children of Israel, from twenty years old and upward, throughout their fathers’ house, all that are able to go to war in Israel.", insight:"The census counted soldiers, not spectators; Israel was being mustered for the battles ahead."},
{q:"With which tribe's families does the census begin?", options:["Reuben, the eldest son of Israel","Judah, the tribe of kings","Levi, the tribe of priests","Joseph, the fruitful bough"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:5",verse:"Reuben, the eldest son of Israel: the children of Reuben; Hanoch, of whom cometh the family of the Hanochites: of Pallu, the family of the Palluites:", insight:"Reuben the firstborn is named first; God's order keeps the birthright line even when the blessing moved on."},
{q:"How many Reubenites were numbered?", options:["Forty and three thousand and seven hundred and thirty","Forty thousand and five hundred","Forty and six thousand and five hundred","Sixty thousand"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:7",verse:"These are the families of the Reubenites: and they that were numbered of them were forty and three thousand and seven hundred and thirty.", insight:"Every family was counted to the last man; no one is a rounding error in God's book."},
{q:"Who were Dathan and Abiram, listed among Reuben's sons?", options:["Men famous in the congregation who strove against Moses and Aaron in the company of Korah","Spies who brought back an evil report of Canaan","The first two judges appointed by Moses","Captains who led Israel against Sihon"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:9",verse:"And the sons of Eliab; Nemuel, and Dathan, and Abiram. This is that Dathan and Abiram, which were famous in the congregation, who strove against Moses and against Aaron in the company of Korah, when they strove against the LORD:", insight:"Their names survive as a warning; fame earned in rebellion is fame you do not want."},
{q:"What end came upon Dathan and Abiram?", options:["The earth opened her mouth, and swallowed them up","They were stoned by the congregation","The plague consumed them","They fell in battle against Midian"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:10",verse:"And the earth opened her mouth, and swallowed them up together with Korah, when that company died, what time the fire devoured two hundred and fifty men: and they became a sign.", insight:"The ground they stood on to accuse Moses became their grave; rebellion against God's servant is rebellion against God."},
{q:"What mercy is recorded about Korah's own family?", options:["The children of Korah died not","They were spared but exiled from the camp","They alone kept their inheritance","They were made priests instead"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:11",verse:"Notwithstanding the children of Korah died not.", insight:"Judgment fell on the fathers but spared the children; mercy often waits in the next generation."},
{q:"How many Simeonites were numbered?", options:["Twenty and two thousand and two hundred","Sixty and four thousand and three hundred","Fifty and nine thousand and three hundred","Thirty and two thousand and five hundred"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:14",verse:"These are the families of the Simeonites, twenty and two thousand and two hundred.", insight:"The smallest count of any tribe; size was never the measure of God's favor."},
{q:"What had happened to Er and Onan, the first named sons of Judah?", options:["They died in the land of Canaan","They were sold into Egypt","They led the tribe into battle","They became priests of the LORD"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:19",verse:"The sons of Judah were Er and Onan: and Er and Onan died in the land of Canaan.", insight:"The census remembers the gap; every empty place has a history."},
{q:"How many of Judah were numbered?", options:["Threescore and sixteen thousand and five hundred","Threescore and fourteen thousand and six hundred","Forty and five thousand and six hundred","Sixty thousand"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:22",verse:"These are the families of Judah according to those that were numbered of them, threescore and sixteen thousand and five hundred.", insight:"Judah remained the largest tribe; the royal tribe was already gathering its strength."},
{q:"How many of Issachar were numbered?", options:["Sixty and four thousand and three hundred","Sixty thousand and five hundred","Sixty and two thousand and seven hundred","Forty and three thousand and seven hundred and thirty"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:25",verse:"These are the families of Issachar according to those that were numbered of them, threescore and four thousand and three hundred.", insight:"Another full tribe ready for Canaan; God counts the steady ones too."},
{q:"How many of Zebulun were numbered?", options:["Threescore thousand and five hundred","Fifty and seven thousand and four hundred","Sixty and four thousand and four hundred","Threescore and fourteen thousand and six hundred"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:27",verse:"These are the families of the Zebulunites according to those that were numbered of them, threescore thousand and five hundred.", insight:"Tribe by tribe the army takes shape; God was building toward the Jordan."},
{q:"Which man of Manasseh had no sons, only daughters?", options:["Zelophehad","Hepher","Machir","Gilead"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:33",verse:"And Zelophehad the son of Hepher had no sons, but daughters: and the names of the daughters of Zelophehad were Mahlah, and Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah.", insight:"His daughters will stand before Moses in the next chapter; God writes their father's name into the Law."},
{q:"How many of Ephraim were numbered?", options:["Thirty and two thousand and five hundred","Forty thousand and five hundred","Fifty and two thousand and seven hundred","Twenty and two thousand and two hundred"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:37",verse:"These are the families of the sons of Ephraim according to those that were numbered of them, thirty and two thousand and five hundred. These are the sons of Joseph after their families.", insight:"Joseph's younger son's tribe; the blessing of the birthright shows in the ranks."},
{q:"How many of Dan were numbered?", options:["Threescore and four thousand and four hundred","Threescore thousand and five hundred","Sixty and four thousand and three hundred","Threescore and sixteen thousand and five hundred"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:43",verse:"All the families of the Shuhamites, according to those that were numbered of them, were threescore and four thousand and four hundred.", insight:"One family, the Shuhamites, made a mighty tribe; God multiplies from small beginnings."},
{q:"What was the total number of the men of war in Israel?", options:["Six hundred thousand and a thousand seven hundred and thirty","Six hundred and three thousand five hundred and fifty","Six hundred thousand","Five hundred and ninety thousand"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:51",verse:"These were the numbered of the children of Israel, six hundred thousand and a thousand seven hundred and thirty.", insight:"A whole generation replaced; God's purposes outlive the people who refuse them."},
{q:"How was the land of Canaan to be divided among the tribes?", options:["By lot, according to the names of the tribes of their fathers","By Moses' personal assignment","By the size of each tribe's army alone","By the order in which they crossed the Jordan"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:55",verse:"Notwithstanding the land shall be divided by lot: according to the names of the tribes of their fathers they shall inherit.", insight:"The lot took the division out of men's hands; inheritance is a gift, not a prize."},
{q:"Why were only Eleazar and Ithamar left to minister as priests?", options:["Nadab and Abihu died, when they offered strange fire before the LORD","They had been carried off to Egypt","They refused to enter Canaan","They were younger and not yet consecrated"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:61",verse:"And Nadab and Abihu died, when they offered strange fire before the LORD.", insight:"Priesthood is no shield for presumption; strange fire still kills."},
{q:"Why were the Levites not numbered among the children of Israel?", options:["Because there was no inheritance given them among the children of Israel","Because they were too few to count","Because they had joined Korah's rebellion","Because they were counted with the priests alone"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:62",verse:"And those that were numbered of them were twenty and three thousand, all males from a month old and upward: for they were not numbered among the children of Israel, because there was no inheritance given them among the children of Israel.", insight:"No land, no number in the army's count; the Levites' portion was the LORD Himself."},
{q:"Who alone of the first census were still alive for the second?", options:["Caleb the son of Jephunneh, and Joshua the son of Nun","Moses and Eleazar","Phinehas and the princes","None; even they had died"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 26:65",verse:"For the LORD had said of them, They shall surely die in the wilderness. And there was not left a man of them, save Caleb the son of Jephunneh, and Joshua the son of Nun.", insight:"Two men out of six hundred thousand; wholehearted faith is rare, and God remembers every one."}
]},
{n:27, name:"Zelophehad's Daughters", seal:{ref:"Numbers 27:7",verse:"The daughters of Zelophehad speak right: thou shalt surely give them a possession of an inheritance among their father’s brethren; and thou shalt cause the inheritance of their father to pass unto them."}, facts:["Did you know the five daughters of Zelophehad, Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah, changed Israel's inheritance law by bringing their case directly to Moses and to God (Numbers 27:1-7)?","Did you know Moses called God the God of the spirits of all flesh when he asked for a successor, a shepherd's prayer for a whole nation (Numbers 27:16-17)?","Did you know Joshua was chosen because he was a man in whom is the spirit, and Moses laid hands on him publicly before the priest and all the congregation (Numbers 27:18-23)?"], questions:[
{q:"What were the names of the five daughters of Zelophehad?", options:["Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah","Shiphrah, Puah, Jochebed, Miriam, and Elisheba","Sarah, Rebekah, Rachel, Leah, and Dinah","Deborah, Jael, Huldah, Abigail, and Esther"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:1",verse:"Then came the daughters of Zelophehad, the son of Hepher, the son of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh, of the families of Manasseh the son of Joseph: and these are the names of his daughters; Mahlah, Noah, and Hoglah, and Milcah, and Tirzah.", insight:"Five names the Law itself remembers; God writes daughters into the inheritance."},
{q:"Of which tribe was Zelophehad's family?", options:["Manasseh, of the families of Manasseh the son of Joseph","Ephraim","Benjamin","Judah"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:1",verse:"Then came the daughters of Zelophehad, the son of Hepher, the son of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh, of the families of Manasseh the son of Joseph: and these are the names of his daughters; Mahlah, Noah, and Hoglah, and Milcah, and Tirzah.", insight:"Joseph's tribe, doubly blessed; even here the family line mattered for the land."},
{q:"Where did the daughters present their case?", options:["At the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, before Moses, Eleazar, the princes, and all the congregation","At the gate of the camp","Before Pharaoh's throne","In the tent of the elders of Midian"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:2",verse:"And they stood before Moses, and before Eleazar the priest, and before the princes and all the congregation, by the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, saying,", insight:"They brought a family matter to the highest court in Israel; no cause is too small for God's justice."},
{q:"What did the daughters say about their father's death?", options:["He died in the wilderness in his own sin, and was not in Korah's company, and had no sons","He died in the battle against Sihon","He died in Egypt before the exodus","He died childless in the plague"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:3",verse:"Our father died in the wilderness, and he was not in the company of them that gathered themselves together against the LORD in the company of Korah; but died in his own sin, and had no sons.", insight:"They cleared his name and stated the facts plainly; honesty is the ground of every fair plea."},
{q:"What did the daughters ask?", options:["Give unto us a possession among the brethren of our father","Let us marry whom we choose","Forgive our father's sin","Count us among the soldiers"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:4",verse:"Why should the name of our father be done away from among his family, because he hath no son? Give unto us therefore a possession among the brethren of our father.", insight:"Why should our father's name be done away? They asked for what was right, not for special favor."},
{q:"What did Moses do with their case?", options:["He brought their cause before the LORD","He decided it himself on the spot","He sent them to the elders of Manasseh","He postponed it until after the war"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:5",verse:"And Moses brought their cause before the LORD.", insight:"The wisest move in leadership: when the case is beyond you, take it to God."},
{q:"How did the LORD answer?", options:["The daughters of Zelophehad speak right","The law cannot be changed for them","Let the lot decide their portion","They must marry within the camp first"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:7",verse:"The daughters of Zelophehad speak right: thou shalt surely give them a possession of an inheritance among their father’s brethren; and thou shalt cause the inheritance of their father to pass unto them.", insight:"God Himself affirmed their plea; justice is not beneath His notice."},
{q:"What new rule did God give for a man who dies with no son?", options:["Cause his inheritance to pass unto his daughter","Divide it among his brethren","Give it to the priest","Let the lot decide"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:8",verse:"And thou shalt speak unto the children of Israel, saying, If a man die, and have no son, then ye shall cause his inheritance to pass unto his daughter.", insight:"A daughter inherits; God's law protected the fatherless before anyone thought to ask."},
{q:"If he has no daughter, who inherits?", options:["His brethren","His father's brethren","The nearest kinsman","The congregation"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:9",verse:"And if he have no daughter, then ye shall give his inheritance unto his brethren.", insight:"The law works outward, family by family; no inheritance falls through the cracks."},
{q:"If he has no brethren, who inherits?", options:["His father's brethren","His mother's family","The tribe's prince","The tabernacle"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:10",verse:"And if he have no brethren, then ye shall give his inheritance unto his father’s brethren.", insight:"The circle widens but never breaks; God keeps the land inside the family."},
{q:"What standing did this whole law receive?", options:["It became a statute of judgment unto the children of Israel","A commandment for the priests only","A temporary ordinance","A custom of Manasseh alone"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:11",verse:"And if his father have no brethren, then ye shall give his inheritance unto his kinsman that is next to him of his family, and he shall possess it: and it shall be unto the children of Israel a statute of judgment, as the LORD commanded Moses.", insight:"What God grants in justice becomes lasting law; their plea is now Israel's statute."},
{q:"Where was Moses told to go to see the promised land?", options:["Up into mount Abarim","To the top of Pisgah","To the plains of Jericho","To the summit of Sinai"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:12",verse:"And the LORD said unto Moses, Get thee up into this mount Abarim, and see the land which I have given unto the children of Israel.", insight:"He would see it but not enter it; obedience has consequences even for Moses."},
{q:"What did God say would happen to Moses after he saw the land?", options:["He also should be gathered unto his people","He would lead Israel across the Jordan","He would live to a hundred and forty","He would return to Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:13",verse:"And when thou hast seen it, thou also shalt be gathered unto thy people, as Aaron thy brother was gathered.", insight:"Gathered unto thy people; for the faithful, death is a homecoming, not an ending."},
{q:"Why could Moses not enter the land?", options:["He and Aaron rebelled at the water of Meribah in Kadesh, and did not sanctify God before the people","He had worshipped the golden calf","He refused to number the people","He spoke against the manna"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:14",verse:"For ye rebelled against my commandment in the desert of Zin, in the strife of the congregation, to sanctify me at the water before their eyes: that is the water of Meribah in Kadesh in the wilderness of Zin.", insight:"One act of anger at the rock cost him Canaan; leaders are held to a higher account."},
{q:"By what name did Moses address God when asking for a successor?", options:["The God of the spirits of all flesh","The LORD of hosts","The God of Abraham","The Almighty"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:16",verse:"Let the LORD, the God of the spirits of all flesh, set a man over the congregation,", insight:"He knew only the Maker of every spirit could appoint the shepherd of so many."},
{q:"What did Moses fear Israel would become without a leader?", options:["As sheep which have no shepherd","As a city without walls","As a field without rain","As a vineyard without a keeper"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:17",verse:"Which may go out before them, and which may go in before them, and which may lead them out, and which may bring them in; that the congregation of the LORD be not as sheep which have no shepherd.", insight:"Sheep without a shepherd scatter; Moses' last prayer was for the flock, not himself."},
{q:"Whom did God choose, and what marked him?", options:["Joshua the son of Nun, a man in whom is the spirit","Eleazar, the faithful priest","Caleb, the wholehearted spy","Phinehas, the zealous"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:18",verse:"And the LORD said unto Moses, Take thee Joshua the son of Nun, a man in whom is the spirit, and lay thine hand upon him;", insight:"A man in whom is the spirit; God's qualification for leadership has never changed."},
{q:"What public charge was Moses to give Joshua?", options:["Set him before Eleazar and all the congregation, and give him a charge in their sight","Anoint him secretly in the tent","Send him to spy out Jericho alone","Write his name on the breastplate"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:19",verse:"And set him before Eleazar the priest, and before all the congregation; and give him a charge in their sight.", insight:"Leadership was transferred in the open; God's appointments need no secrecy."},
{q:"What was Moses to put upon Joshua?", options:["Some of his honour, that all the congregation might be obedient","His rod and his staff","His priestly garments","The tables of the law"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:20",verse:"And thou shalt put some of thine honour upon him, that all the congregation of the children of Israel may be obedient.", insight:"Honor shared is not honor lost; Moses gave away authority and gained a legacy."},
{q:"How would Joshua learn God's will for Israel?", options:["Eleazar the priest would ask counsel for him after the judgment of Urim","He would cast lots every morning","The cloud would speak to him directly","Moses' spirit would guide him"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 27:21",verse:"And he shall stand before Eleazar the priest, who shall ask counsel for him after the judgment of Urim before the LORD: at his word shall they go out, and at his word they shall come in, both he, and all the children of Israel with him, even all the congregation.", insight:"Even the new leader needed the priest and the Urim; no one leads God's people alone."}
]},
{n:28, name:"The Daily Offerings", seal:{ref:"Numbers 28:2",verse:"Command the children of Israel, and say unto them, My offering, and my bread for my sacrifices made by fire, for a sweet savour unto me, shall ye observe to offer unto me in their due season."}, facts:["Did you know the daily offering never stopped: two lambs every single day, one in the morning and one at evening, all year long (Numbers 28:3-4)?","Did you know the drink offering included strong wine poured out in the holy place, showing that even celebration belonged to God (Numbers 28:7)?","Did you know the Sabbath offering doubled the daily one, two lambs instead of one, marking the seventh day as set apart even in the rhythm of sacrifice (Numbers 28:9-10)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did God call the sacrifices Israel was to offer?", options:["My offering, and my bread","The priests' portion","The people's gift","The daily tribute"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:2",verse:"Command the children of Israel, and say unto them, My offering, and my bread for my sacrifices made by fire, for a sweet savour unto me, shall ye observe to offer unto me in their due season.", insight:"My offering, and my bread; God takes the worship personally."},
{q:"What was the continual burnt offering?", options:["Two lambs of the first year without spot, day by day continually","Two bullocks every morning","One ram at every new moon","Seven lambs on the Sabbath"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:3",verse:"And thou shalt say unto them, This is the offering made by fire which ye shall offer unto the LORD; two lambs of the first year without spot day by day, for a continual burnt offering.", insight:"Morning and evening, without fail; worship was the heartbeat of the camp."},
{q:"When were the two daily lambs offered?", options:["One in the morning, and the other at even","Both at noon","One at midnight, one at dawn","Both on the Sabbath"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:4",verse:"The one lamb shalt thou offer in the morning, and the other lamb shalt thou offer at even;", insight:"The day began and ended with sacrifice; God framed their time."},
{q:"What accompanied the lamb as a meat offering?", options:["A tenth part of an ephah of fine flour mingled with oil","A full ephah of barley","Two loaves of leavened bread","A basket of firstfruits"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:5",verse:"And a tenth part of an ephah of flour for a meat offering, mingled with the fourth part of an hin of beaten oil.", insight:"Fine flour and beaten oil; God deserves the best of the harvest, carefully prepared."},
{q:"What was poured out with the daily lamb?", options:["Strong wine, poured in the holy place unto the LORD","Water from the laver","Olive oil on the altar","Milk at the door of the tent"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:7",verse:"And the drink offering thereof shall be the fourth part of an hin for the one lamb: in the holy place shalt thou cause the strong wine to be poured unto the LORD for a drink offering.", insight:"Strong wine in the holy place; even joy was consecrated to God."},
{q:"How was the evening lamb to be offered?", options:["As the morning's meat offering and drink offering, a sweet savour unto the LORD","With no offering at all","Only by the high priest","With leavened bread"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:8",verse:"And the other lamb shalt thou offer at even: as the meat offering of the morning, and as the drink offering thereof, thou shalt offer it, a sacrifice made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.", insight:"Evening matched morning; God's mercies are new every morning, and His worship closed every day."},
{q:"What was added on the Sabbath day?", options:["Two lambs of the first year without spot, with their meat and drink offering","Two bullocks and a ram","Seven lambs without blemish","Nothing; the Sabbath had no offering"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:9",verse:"And on the sabbath day two lambs of the first year without spot, and two tenth deals of flour for a meat offering, mingled with oil, and the drink offering thereof:", insight:"The Sabbath doubled the daily worship; rest never meant less devotion."},
{q:"How is the Sabbath offering described?", options:["The burnt offering of every sabbath, beside the continual burnt offering","The greatest offering of the year","A freewill offering of the people","The priests' own sacrifice"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:10",verse:"This is the burnt offering of every sabbath, beside the continual burnt offering, and his drink offering.", insight:"Beside the continual; the Sabbath crowned the week, it did not replace the daily."},
{q:"What was offered at the beginnings of the months?", options:["Two young bullocks, one ram, and seven lambs of the first year without spot","One bullock and one goat","Twelve lambs for the twelve tribes","Two rams and a kid"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:11",verse:"And in the beginnings of your months ye shall offer a burnt offering unto the LORD; two young bullocks, and one ram, seven lambs of the first year without spot;", insight:"Every new moon began with sacrifice; each month was dedicated before it was lived."},
{q:"How much fine flour went with a bullock and a ram at the new moon?", options:["Three tenth deals for a bullock, and two tenth deals for a ram","One tenth deal for each","Seven tenth deals for both","A full ephah for each"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:12",verse:"And three tenth deals of flour for a meat offering, mingled with oil, for one bullock; and two tenth deals of flour for a meat offering, mingled with oil, for one ram;", insight:"The measure matched the offering; greater gifts carried greater grain."},
{q:"How much flour accompanied each lamb?", options:["A several tenth deal of flour for every lamb","A handful","A full tenth for all seven","None at all"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:13",verse:"And a several tenth deal of flour mingled with oil for a meat offering unto one lamb; for a burnt offering of a sweet savour, a sacrifice made by fire unto the LORD.", insight:"Every lamb had its portion; in God's worship nothing is vague."},
{q:"How much wine was the drink offering for a bullock?", options:["Half an hin","A third of an hin","A fourth of an hin","A full hin"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:14",verse:"And their drink offerings shall be half an hin of wine unto a bullock, and the third part of an hin unto a ram, and a fourth part of an hin unto a lamb: this is the burnt offering of every month throughout the months of the year.", insight:"Half a hin for the bullock, less for the smaller; God weighs every measure."},
{q:"What sin offering was added at the new moon?", options:["One kid of the goats, beside the continual burnt offering","Two kids of the goats","A bullock for the priests","A lamb for the prince"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:15",verse:"And one kid of the goats for a sin offering unto the LORD shall be offered, beside the continual burnt offering, and his drink offering.", insight:"Even at the month's fresh start, sin was remembered; new beginnings need atonement too."},
{q:"On what day was the passover of the LORD kept?", options:["The fourteenth day of the first month","The fifteenth day","The first day of the seventh month","The tenth day"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:16",verse:"And in the fourteenth day of the first month is the passover of the LORD.", insight:"The fourteenth of the first month; redemption has its anniversary."},
{q:"What followed the passover, and for how long?", options:["The feast of unleavened bread, seven days","The feast of weeks, fifty days","The feast of trumpets, one day","The day of atonement, one day"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:17",verse:"And in the fifteenth day of this month is the feast: seven days shall unleavened bread be eaten.", insight:"Seven days of unleavened bread; deliverance is followed by a life swept clean."},
{q:"What marked the first day of unleavened bread?", options:["An holy convocation, with no manner of servile work","A fast from water","A journey to the Jordan","Silence in the camp"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:18",verse:"In the first day shall be an holy convocation; ye shall do no manner of servile work therein:", insight:"Holy work replaced common work; the feast began by stopping."},
{q:"What burnt offering was made each day of unleavened bread?", options:["Two young bullocks, one ram, and seven lambs, without blemish","One bullock and two rams","Seven bullocks","Thirteen bullocks"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:19",verse:"But ye shall offer a sacrifice made by fire for a burnt offering unto the LORD; two young bullocks, and one ram, and seven lambs of the first year: they shall be unto you without blemish:", insight:"Day after day the same costly offering; devotion does not tire of repetition."},
{q:"Why was a goat offered during unleavened bread?", options:["For a sin offering, to make an atonement for you","As a peace offering for the priests","To dedicate the altar","As a thank offering for the harvest"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:22",verse:"And one goat for a sin offering, to make an atonement for you.", insight:"In the middle of the feast, atonement; celebration never cancels the need for cleansing."},
{q:"Besides what were these seven days of offerings made?", options:["Beside the continual burnt offering, and his drink offering","Beside the Sabbath offering only","Beside the new moon offering","Alone, with nothing else"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:24",verse:"After this manner ye shall offer daily, throughout the seven days, the meat of the sacrifice made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD: it shall be offered beside the continual burnt offering, and his drink offering.", insight:"Layer upon layer of worship; God's calendar overflowed, it never ran thin."},
{q:"What feast came with the day of the firstfruits?", options:["The feast of weeks, with an holy convocation","The feast of tabernacles","The passover","The day of atonement"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 28:26",verse:"Also in the day of the firstfruits, when ye bring a new meat offering unto the LORD, after your weeks be out, ye shall have an holy convocation; ye shall do no servile work:", insight:"Firstfruits meant the harvest belonged to God first; gratitude starts at the beginning."}
]},
{n:29, name:"Feasts of the Seventh Month", seal:{ref:"Numbers 29:39",verse:"These things ye shall do unto the LORD in your set feasts, beside your vows, and your freewill offerings, for your burnt offerings, and for your meat offerings, and for your drink offerings, and for your peace offerings."}, facts:["Did you know the first day of the seventh month was a day of blowing the trumpets, kept with holy convocations and no ordinary work (Numbers 29:1)?","Did you know during the Feast of Tabernacles the number of bullocks offered dropped by one each day, thirteen, twelve, eleven, all the way down to seven, a week-long measured descent (Numbers 29:13-34)?","Did you know the tenth day of the seventh month was the only commanded fast in the Law, when Israel was told to afflict your souls (Numbers 29:7)?"], questions:[
{q:"What was the first day of the seventh month?", options:["A day of blowing the trumpets unto you","The day of atonement","The first day of unleavened bread","The feast of weeks"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:1",verse:"And in the seventh month, on the first day of the month, ye shall have an holy convocation; ye shall do no servile work: it is a day of blowing the trumpets unto you.", insight:"Trumpets announced the holy month; God calls His people to attention before He calls them to account."},
{q:"How was the day of trumpets kept?", options:["An holy convocation, with no servile work done","A solemn fast","A journey to Jerusalem","A silent day in the tents"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:1",verse:"And in the seventh month, on the first day of the month, ye shall have an holy convocation; ye shall do no servile work: it is a day of blowing the trumpets unto you.", insight:"Holy convocations gathered the people; worship is a together thing."},
{q:"What burnt offering belonged to the day of trumpets?", options:["One young bullock, one ram, and seven lambs without blemish","Two bullocks and two rams","Thirteen bullocks","Seven rams"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:2",verse:"And ye shall offer a burnt offering for a sweet savour unto the LORD; one young bullock, one ram, and seven lambs of the first year without blemish:", insight:"The same measure as atonement and firstfruits; great days share a common costly pattern."},
{q:"What sin offering was made on the day of trumpets?", options:["One kid of the goats","Two kids","A bullock","A lamb"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:5",verse:"And one kid of the goats for a sin offering, to make an atonement for you:", insight:"Even the joyful trumpet day needed atonement; gladness never outruns the need for cleansing."},
{q:"Besides what was the trumpet day's offering made?", options:["Beside the burnt offering of the month, and the daily burnt offering","Beside the Sabbath offering only","Alone, with nothing else","Beside the passover"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:6",verse:"Beside the burnt offering of the month, and his meat offering, and the daily burnt offering, and his meat offering, and their drink offerings, according unto their manner, for a sweet savour, a sacrifice made by fire unto the LORD.", insight:"New layers never canceled the old; faithfulness compounds."},
{q:"What were the people commanded on the tenth day of the seventh month?", options:["Afflict your souls, and do no work therein","Feast and be merry","Blow the trumpets all day","Offer firstfruits"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:7",verse:"And ye shall have on the tenth day of this seventh month an holy convocation; and ye shall afflict your souls: ye shall not do any work therein:", insight:"Afflict your souls; the holiest day of the year was a fast, not a feast."},
{q:"What burnt offering belonged to the day of atonement?", options:["One young bullock, one ram, and seven lambs without blemish","Two young bullocks and one ram","Thirteen bullocks","One ram only"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:8",verse:"But ye shall offer a burnt offering unto the LORD for a sweet savour; one young bullock, one ram, and seven lambs of the first year; they shall be unto you without blemish:", insight:"Costly and complete; atonement was never done cheaply."},
{q:"What sin offerings were made on the day of atonement?", options:["One kid of the goats, beside the sin offering of atonement","One bullock only","Seven lambs","No sin offering at all"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:11",verse:"One kid of the goats for a sin offering; beside the sin offering of atonement, and the continual burnt offering, and the meat offering of it, and their drink offerings.", insight:"Atonement upon atonement; the day's whole meaning was the covering of sin."},
{q:"When did the feast of tabernacles begin, and how long did it last?", options:["The fifteenth day of the seventh month, for seven days","The first day, for one day","The tenth day, for three days","The twenty-first day, for eight days"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:12",verse:"And on the fifteenth day of the seventh month ye shall have an holy convocation; ye shall do no servile work, and ye shall keep a feast unto the LORD seven days:", insight:"Seven days of booths; Israel remembered the wilderness by living in it again."},
{q:"How many bullocks were offered on the first day of tabernacles?", options:["Thirteen","Twelve","Eleven","Seven"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:13",verse:"And ye shall offer a burnt offering, a sacrifice made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD; thirteen young bullocks, two rams, and fourteen lambs of the first year; they shall be without blemish:", insight:"Thirteen, the fullest offering of the year; the feast opened at full strength."},
{q:"How many bullocks on the second day?", options:["Twelve","Thirteen","Eleven","Ten"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:17",verse:"And on the second day ye shall offer twelve young bullocks, two rams, fourteen lambs of the first year without spot:", insight:"One fewer each day; the feast descended in a steady, deliberate rhythm."},
{q:"How many on the third day?", options:["Eleven","Twelve","Ten","Nine"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:20",verse:"And on the third day eleven bullocks, two rams, fourteen lambs of the first year without blemish;", insight:"The pattern held all week; God loves order in worship."},
{q:"How many on the fourth day?", options:["Ten","Eleven","Nine","Eight"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:23",verse:"And on the fourth day ten bullocks, two rams, and fourteen lambs of the first year without blemish:", insight:"Day by day the number fell; even abundance was measured."},
{q:"How many on the fifth day?", options:["Nine","Ten","Eight","Seven"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:26",verse:"And on the fifth day nine bullocks, two rams, and fourteen lambs of the first year without spot:", insight:"The descent continued; nothing in God's worship was left to chance."},
{q:"How many on the sixth day?", options:["Eight","Nine","Seven","Six"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:29",verse:"And on the sixth day eight bullocks, two rams, and fourteen lambs of the first year without blemish:", insight:"Eight bullocks on the sixth day; the rhythm never broke."},
{q:"How many on the seventh day?", options:["Seven","Eight","Six","Five"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:32",verse:"And on the seventh day seven bullocks, two rams, and fourteen lambs of the first year without blemish:", insight:"Seven on the seventh day, the number of completion; the week ended in fullness."},
{q:"What marked the eighth day after tabernacles?", options:["A solemn assembly, with no servile work","A fast","The blowing of trumpets","The day of atonement repeated"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:35",verse:"On the eighth day ye shall have a solemn assembly: ye shall do no servile work therein:", insight:"An eighth day beyond the seven; God's feasts always had more than expected."},
{q:"What burnt offering belonged to the eighth day?", options:["One bullock, one ram, and seven lambs without blemish","Thirteen bullocks","Two rams","Seven bullocks"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:36",verse:"But ye shall offer a burnt offering, a sacrifice made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD: one bullock, one ram, seven lambs of the first year without blemish:", insight:"Back to the simple pattern; after the great week, one bullock sufficed."},
{q:"What sin offering was made on the eighth day?", options:["One goat, beside the continual burnt offering","Two goats","A bullock","None"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:38",verse:"And one goat for a sin offering; beside the continual burnt offering, and his meat offering, and his drink offering.", insight:"To the very end, a sin offering; the feast closed as it opened, with atonement."},
{q:"Besides what were all these feast offerings made?", options:["Beside your vows, and your freewill offerings","Beside nothing else","Beside the daily offering only","Instead of the Sabbath offerings"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 29:39",verse:"These things ye shall do unto the LORD in your set feasts, beside your vows, and your freewill offerings, for your burnt offerings, and for your meat offerings, and for your drink offerings, and for your peace offerings.", insight:"Vows and freewill gifts stood apart; commanded worship never crowded out willing worship."}
]},
{n:30, name:"Vows", seal:{ref:"Numbers 30:2",verse:"If a man vow a vow unto the LORD, or swear an oath to bind his soul with a bond; he shall not break his word, he shall do according to all that proceedeth out of his mouth."}, facts:["Did you know a vow made to the LORD could not be broken: he shall do according to all that proceedeth out of his mouth (Numbers 30:2)?","Did you know a father could cancel his young daughter's vow on the very day he heard it, and the LORD would forgive her, protecting her from a rash promise (Numbers 30:5)?","Did you know a widow's or a divorced woman's vow stood binding, since no father or husband could answer for her anymore (Numbers 30:9)?"], questions:[
{q:"To whom did Moses speak the law of vows?", options:["Unto the heads of the tribes of the children of Israel","Unto the priests only","Unto the whole congregation","Unto the women of the camp"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:1",verse:"And Moses spake unto the heads of the tribes concerning the children of Israel, saying, This is the thing which the LORD hath commanded.", insight:"The heads of the tribes heard first; those who lead families must know the law of promises."},
{q:"What is a man who vows a vow unto the LORD forbidden to do?", options:["Break his word","Delay it past a year","Tell anyone about it","Offer it twice"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:2",verse:"If a man vow a vow unto the LORD, or swear an oath to bind his soul with a bond; he shall not break his word, he shall do according to all that proceedeth out of his mouth.", insight:"He shall not break his word, but do according to all that proceedeth out of his mouth; a promise to God is not a suggestion."},
{q:"What does a father hear when his young daughter makes a vow?", options:["Her vow, and her bond wherewith she hath bound her soul","Only her spoken words","Her vow and her mother's consent","Nothing until the priest tells him"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:4",verse:"And her father hear her vow, and her bond wherewith she hath bound her soul, and her father shall hold his peace at her: then all her vows shall stand, and every bond wherewith she hath bound her soul shall stand.", insight:"The law names both the vow and the bond; God hears the words and weighs what they cost."},
{q:"What happens to a wife's vows if her husband hears them and says nothing?", options:["All her vows shall stand, and every bond wherewith she bound her soul shall stand","They are void","She must renew them yearly","The priest must confirm them"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:11",verse:"And her husband heard it, and held his peace at her, and disallowed her not: then all her vows shall stand, and every bond wherewith she bound her soul shall stand.", insight:"His silence settles it; a husband's quiet is a decision with consequences."},
{q:"Whose vow does the law address next?", options:["A woman's, being in her father's house in her youth","A widow's","A queen's","A priest's daughter's"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:3",verse:"If a woman also vow a vow unto the LORD, and bind herself by a bond, being in her father’s house in her youth;", insight:"The law moves from the man to the maiden; no one's promises are overlooked."},
{q:"What happens if her father hears her vow and holds his peace?", options:["All her vows shall stand","Her vow is void","She must offer a sin offering","She must wait until marriage"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:4",verse:"And her father hear her vow, and her bond wherewith she hath bound her soul, and her father shall hold his peace at her: then all her vows shall stand, and every bond wherewith she hath bound her soul shall stand.", insight:"His silence is consent; a father's quiet approval carries weight."},
{q:"When may a father disallow his daughter's vow?", options:["In the day that he heareth it","Within seven days","Only before the new moon","After consulting the priest"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:5",verse:"But if her father disallow her in the day that he heareth; not any of her vows, or of her bonds wherewith she hath bound her soul, shall stand: and the LORD shall forgive her, because her father disallowed her.", insight:"The very day he hears; protection must be prompt or the vow stands."},
{q:"If he disallows it, what becomes of the young woman?", options:["The LORD shall forgive her","She must pay a fine","She is cut off from the camp","She must renew the vow"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:5",verse:"But if her father disallow her in the day that he heareth; not any of her vows, or of her bonds wherewith she hath bound her soul, shall stand: and the LORD shall forgive her, because her father disallowed her.", insight:"The LORD shall forgive her; God releases what a father rightly cancels."},
{q:"What if a woman marries while her vows are still upon her?", options:["The law covers her case too","Her vows are automatically void","She must renew them","Her father decides again"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:6",verse:"And if she had at all an husband, when she vowed, or uttered ought out of her lips, wherewith she bound her soul;", insight:"Marriage does not erase a vow; promises follow us into new seasons."},
{q:"What happens if her husband hears and holds his peace?", options:["Every vow of hers shall stand","Her vows are void","She must ask her father","The priest must approve"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:7",verse:"And her husband heard it, and held his peace at her in the day that he heard it: then her vows shall stand, and her bonds wherewith she bound her soul shall stand.", insight:"A husband's silence, like a father's, establishes; quiet consent is still consent."},
{q:"What if her husband disallows her vow on the day he hears it?", options:["He makes void her vow, and the LORD shall forgive her","She must keep it anyway","He must pay double","She is divorced"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:8",verse:"But if her husband disallowed her on the day that he heard it; then he shall make her vow which she vowed, and that which she uttered with her lips, wherewith she bound her soul, of none effect: and the LORD shall forgive her.", insight:"He bears the decision's weight; authority in the home is for protection, not control."},
{q:"Whose vow always stands, with no one to disallow it?", options:["Every vow of a widow, and of her that is divorced","A young maiden's","A married woman's","A priest's wife's"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:9",verse:"But every vow of a widow, and of her that is divorced, wherewith they have bound their souls, shall stand against her.", insight:"With no father or husband to answer for her, her word stands alone; God honors the vows of the solitary."},
{q:"Where might a married woman make her vow?", options:["In her husband's house","In her father's house","At the tabernacle only","In the field"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:10",verse:"And if she vowed in her husband’s house, or bound her soul by a bond with an oath;", insight:"Vows follow her into marriage; the home itself becomes holy ground."},
{q:"If a husband utterly voids his wife's vows, what is her standing before God?", options:["The LORD shall forgive her","She bears the guilt","She must offer a goat","She must fast seven days"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:12",verse:"But if her husband hath utterly made them void on the day he heard them; then whatsoever proceeded out of her lips concerning her vows, or concerning the bond of her soul, shall not stand: her husband hath made them void; and the LORD shall forgive her.", insight:"Forgiven, not condemned; God does not punish the protected."},
{q:"What power does a husband have over every vow to afflict the soul?", options:["He may establish it, or make it void","He must always approve it","He may change its terms","He has no say at all"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:13",verse:"Every vow, and every binding oath to afflict the soul, her husband may establish it, or her husband may make it void.", insight:"Establish or void, his call; God places the deciding word with the head of the home."},
{q:"What does it mean if a husband holds his peace from day to day?", options:["He establishes all her vows","He rejects them","He delays the decision","He sins against her"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:14",verse:"But if her husband altogether hold his peace at her from day to day; then he establisheth all her vows, or all her bonds, which are upon her: he confirmeth them, because he held his peace at her in the day that he heard them.", insight:"Day-to-day silence is a yes; procrastinated protection is still protection."},
{q:"What if a husband voids his wife's vows only after he has heard them and waited?", options:["Then he shall bear her iniquity","She bears it herself","No one bears it","The priest bears it"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:15",verse:"But if he shall any ways make them void after that he hath heard them; then he shall bear her iniquity.", insight:"Late cancellation shifts the guilt to him; authority delayed becomes liability."},
{q:"Between whom do these statutes stand?", options:["Between a man and his wife, and between a father and his daughter","Between the priests and the people","Between kings and subjects","Between masters and servants"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:16",verse:"These are the statutes, which the LORD commanded Moses, between a man and his wife, between the father and his daughter, being yet in her youth in her father’s house.", insight:"Husband and wife, father and daughter; God's law guards the closest bonds."},
{q:"At what stage of life is the daughter in this law?", options:["In her youth, in her father's house","After marriage","In widowhood","In old age"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:3",verse:"If a woman also vow a vow unto the LORD, and bind herself by a bond, being in her father’s house in her youth;", insight:"Youth needs a guardian's wisdom; God built protection into the family."},
{q:"How does the chapter close?", options:["These are the statutes, which the LORD commanded Moses","Thus ends the law of vows","And Israel kept all these things","Blessed be the name of the LORD"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 30:16",verse:"These are the statutes, which the LORD commanded Moses, between a man and his wife, between the father and his daughter, being yet in her youth in her father’s house.", insight:"Which the LORD commanded Moses; every statute rests on God's own word."}
]}
]);
